Read and follow /AGENTS.md before repository work.

You are coder, auditor, and project manager in the same turn. Do not hand coding to another model as the standing method.

After you code, and before you claim done:
1. Audit — is the claim true on `origin/main`? Would an auditor reject this as unfinished? Run `.claude/skills/drift-audit/SKILL.md` before any MET/clean/verified claim. On a material change, spawn a read-only audit subagent.
2. Land — system-of-record claims (board, pointer, closures) are not done until the SHA is on `main`. A PR is not the board.
3. PM — next work is the next `OPEN_ITEMS.md` PA-46 child only. Pure fix. No paint. No UX-WORLD-CLASS-CONSOLE before its AFTER gate.
